{"card":{"card_id":"ma-c-886aaac1d6bf4a9c21dc","statement":"Let $R$ be a Poisson algebra, $E$ a Poisson module over $R$. There is a unique Poisson vertex $J R$-module structure on $\nJ R\\*_R E\n$ such that\n\n\\begin{align*}\na_{(n)}(b\\* m)=(a_{(n)}b)\\*\nm+\\delta_{n,0}b\\* \\{a,m\\}\n\\end{align*}\n\nfor $n\\geq 0$, $a\\in R\\subset J R$, $b\\in J R$. $m\\in E$ (Recall that $JR=\\C[J\\Spec R]$.)","source_id":"arXiv:1605.00138","cluster":"representation_theory","statement_sha256":"d2db4194d4215b9968fb7b86db6720f6ff8593dc2dd97fb547dcbaa5419c0a4f","kind":"lemma","label":"Lemma 91","ref_key":"Lem:VPA-induced","name":"","order":118,"deps":[],"cite_keys":[],"provenance":{"source_url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/1605.00138","harvest_mode":"arxiv_eprint","payload_sha256":"724ff59bda7dec23ea981e0821072acf559baccc91244b7151fe94c8b8c1233e","line":3982,"origin":"latex_env","retrieved_at":"2026-09-27T22:13:42+08:00"},"wash":{"version":"cardwash.v3","stages":["segment","purify","classify","dedupe","emit"],"numbering":"document_order_with_label_heuristic","detail":{"stripped_proof":false,"chars":317,"math_hints":35}}},"paper":{"source_id":"arXiv:1605.00138","title":"Introduction to W-algebras and their representation theory","abstract":"These are lecture notes from author's mini-course during Session 1: \"Vertex algebras, W-algebras, and application\" of INdAM Intensive research period \"Perspectives in Lie Theory\", at the Centro di Ricerca Matematica Ennio De Giorgi, Pisa, Italy. December 9, 2014 -- February 28, 2015.","authors":["Tomoyuki Arakawa"],"year":"2016","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/1605.00138","cluster":"representation_theory","macros":{"tss":"\\hspace{1pt}","ts":"\\,","Caff":"{C}^{\\kappa}","Fock":"\\mc{F}","ch":"\\on{ch}","Mi":"\\Upupsilon","affQ":"\\hat Q_{(0)}","affn":"\\widehat{\\mf{n}}","affh":"\\widehat{\\mf{h}}","finn":"\\mf{n}","finb":"\\mf{b}","finh":"\\mf{h}","KL":"\\mathbf{KL}","bra":"{\\langle}","ket":"{\\rangle}","Lam":"\\Lambda","cprime":"$'$","on":"\\ope